option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow quality
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Texels of the sun's shadow map. The RTS view fits the map to what is on screen, so it is sharpest zoomed in.
option.shadowDistance=Shadow distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far round the camera shadow casters are drawn, in blocks. Less is faster.
option.sunPathRotation=Sun tilt
option.sunPathRotation.comment=Tilts the sun's path so noon still throws shadows you can see from above (30 = lovish's pick).
option.HAZE_STRENGTH=Distance haze
option.HAZE_STRENGTH.comment=How much air shows over distant ground (1 = the game's own look).
option.SOFT_SHADOWS=Soft shadows
option.SOFT_SHADOWS.comment=Shadows are sharp where they meet their caster and soften the farther they fall, as real sunlight does. Off: crisp edges everywhere (a little faster).
value.SOFT_SHADOWS.0=Off
value.SOFT_SHADOWS.1=On
option.AO=Ambient occlusion
option.AO.comment=Building bases, wall corners and unit feet sit in the ground: creases see less sky, so they lose part of the sky's light (never the sun's).
value.AO.0=Off
value.AO.1=On
option.AO_STRENGTH=Occlusion strength
option.AO_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the creases get (1 = the tuned look; the darkest is capped so units in alleys stay readable).
option.GRADE=Colour grade
option.GRADE.comment=Enchanted: a little dimmer, richer colour, golden light, a soft glow. Off: the tone curve only.
value.GRADE.0=Off
value.GRADE.1=Enchanted
option.EDGE_AA=Edge smoothing
option.EDGE_AA.comment=Smooths unit and building edges without softening textures.
value.EDGE_AA.0=Off
value.EDGE_AA.1=On
option.MATERIALS=Material maps
option.MATERIALS.comment=Reads our blocks' and units' surface maps: relief, metal and gem highlights, glowing parts. Off: flat surfaces, as before.
value.MATERIALS.0=Off
value.MATERIALS.1=On
